1
00:00:00,708 --> 00:00:02,416
[portal powering up]

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:04,458
Come on, we gotta--

3
00:00:04,458 --> 00:00:05,333
Whoa!

4
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:07,250
[zombie-like moaning]

5
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:08,958
Fritz and Spitz?

6
00:00:08,958 --> 00:00:10,583
Oh, no!

7
00:00:10,583 --> 00:00:11,833
They're hollow!

8
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:14,875
Those spectral jerk-faces
attacked the Monastery!

9
00:00:14,875 --> 00:00:17,666
No one attacked the Monastery,
Wyldfyre.

10
00:00:17,666 --> 00:00:20,208
But can't say the same
for the Land of Lost Things.

11
00:00:20,208 --> 00:00:21,875
Do you know
what happened to them?

12
00:00:21,875 --> 00:00:23,958
Yeah,
the same thing is happening

13
00:00:23,958 --> 00:00:24,958
all over the place.

14
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:26,250
[Riyu yelping]

15
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:28,250
[Sora laughing]

16
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:30,125
Aw, I missed you too, Riyu.

17
00:00:30,125 --> 00:00:32,041
[grumbling affectionately]

18
00:00:32,041 --> 00:00:34,708
I know, I'm sorry I left,

19
00:00:34,708 --> 00:00:37,333
but I had to make sure
Arin was okay.

20
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:38,875
[grumbling curiously]

21
00:00:38,875 --> 00:00:41,625
And he'll be back
to see you too.

22
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:42,916
[grumbling joyfully]

23
00:00:42,916 --> 00:00:45,541
So people are
getting drained like this

24
00:00:45,541 --> 00:00:47,583
outside of
the Land of Lost Things?

25
00:00:47,583 --> 00:00:49,000
It's ThunderFang...

26
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,500
using the Forbidden Five
to collect souls,

27
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,458
trying to become
a Source Dragon.

28
00:00:53,458 --> 00:00:55,333
Tell me there's a plan.

29
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:57,000
The Ninja always have a plan.

30
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,041
We do,

31
00:00:58,041 --> 00:00:59,583
but it's wild.

32
00:00:59,583 --> 00:01:03,250
[zombie-like groaning]

33
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:05,375
[spectral shrieking]

34
00:01:05,375 --> 00:01:06,708
[roaring]

35
00:01:09,916 --> 00:01:11,875
[ThunderFang cackling]

36
00:01:11,875 --> 00:01:14,958
[evil laughter]

37
00:01:14,958 --> 00:01:16,750
[Lloyd] So we take
that thing to the well

38
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:18,541
where ThunderFang's energy's
coming from,

39
00:01:18,541 --> 00:01:19,708
and once the other teams

40
00:01:19,708 --> 00:01:22,041
wake up their halves
of the Arc Dragon of Focus,

41
00:01:22,041 --> 00:01:23,791
it'll be summoned
right to our spot.

42
00:01:23,791 --> 00:01:25,916
Piece of cake! Day saved.

43
00:01:25,916 --> 00:01:27,458
Uh, night saved.

44
00:01:27,458 --> 00:01:29,791
"Piece of cake"? Really?

45
00:01:29,791 --> 00:01:31,791
That's even optimistic for me.

46
00:01:31,791 --> 00:01:33,333
Trying to get psyched up.

47
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:35,041
Yes, this will be hard,

48
00:01:35,041 --> 00:01:37,125
but if we start thinking
it's impossible,

49
00:01:37,125 --> 00:01:38,833
we don't stand a chance.

50
00:01:48,291 --> 00:01:50,041
Uh, you take this thing.

51
00:01:50,041 --> 00:01:50,958
I'm gonna mess it up.

52
00:01:50,958 --> 00:01:52,291
Why would you mess it up?

53
00:01:52,291 --> 00:01:53,666
[sighing] Come on,

54
00:01:53,666 --> 00:01:55,791
messing things up
is what I do best.

55
00:01:55,791 --> 00:01:58,041
It's basically
my elemental power.

56
00:01:58,041 --> 00:02:00,333
You think I started out
with skills?

57
00:02:00,333 --> 00:02:01,541
Uh, yeah.

58
00:02:01,541 --> 00:02:03,625
You're the Legendary
Green Ninja.

59
00:02:03,625 --> 00:02:05,666
You didn't know me as a kid.

60
00:02:05,666 --> 00:02:07,250
There were
plenty of reasons to think

61
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:08,625
I'd never be a Ninja,

62
00:02:08,625 --> 00:02:11,916
but confidence
is just another skill to build.

63
00:02:11,916 --> 00:02:13,125
Someday,

64
00:02:13,125 --> 00:02:15,125
you're going to be
one of the greatest Ninja

65
00:02:15,125 --> 00:02:16,083
to ever live.

66
00:02:16,083 --> 00:02:18,041
No, I'm not.

67
00:02:18,041 --> 00:02:20,875
Lloyd, I finally have
my parents,

68
00:02:20,875 --> 00:02:24,125
and the Land of Lee is filled
with other kids' parents,

69
00:02:24,125 --> 00:02:26,541
other peoples' loved ones.

70
00:02:26,541 --> 00:02:28,000
I came here with you

71
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,166
to release their souls
from ThunderFang,

72
00:02:30,166 --> 00:02:33,458
to help reunite families
like mine,

73
00:02:33,458 --> 00:02:35,750
but when this is all over...

74
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:37,458
I'm quitting the Ninja.

75
00:02:38,958 --> 00:02:42,083
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

76
00:02:42,083 --> 00:02:45,166
♪ Together we will rise ♪

77
00:02:45,166 --> 00:02:48,625
♪ We fight ♪

78
00:02:48,625 --> 00:02:51,708
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

79
00:02:58,041 --> 00:02:59,333
[grunting with impact]

80
00:02:59,333 --> 00:03:00,458
[exhaling]

81
00:03:02,416 --> 00:03:03,416
What the--?

82
00:03:04,541 --> 00:03:05,541
[sighing]

83
00:03:05,541 --> 00:03:06,666
Weird.

84
00:03:06,666 --> 00:03:09,083
Well, that's Mysterium for ya.

85
00:03:09,083 --> 00:03:10,208
Hmm.

86
00:03:10,208 --> 00:03:11,583
All right,

87
00:03:11,583 --> 00:03:14,000
as long as Bleckt's directions
to the cave are accurate,

88
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,375
I got this.

89
00:03:16,416 --> 00:03:19,375
Yup, I got this.

90
00:03:19,375 --> 00:03:20,625
Don't need anyone else.

91
00:03:20,625 --> 00:03:22,583
Definitely not Jay.
[chuckling]

92
00:03:22,583 --> 00:03:24,583
I mean, forget about me and him,

93
00:03:24,583 --> 00:03:26,083
what about being a Ninja?

94
00:03:26,083 --> 00:03:29,000
How is being a mercenary
who cares only about money

95
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,083
more exciting?

96
00:03:30,083 --> 00:03:31,000
Hello?

97
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,666
Ninja!

98
00:03:32,666 --> 00:03:34,791
You're talking
to yourself again, Nya.

99
00:03:34,791 --> 00:03:36,541
[sighing] Anyway...

100
00:03:36,541 --> 00:03:37,958
Cave of Tones!

101
00:03:39,458 --> 00:03:41,875
[pounding against door]

102
00:03:41,875 --> 00:03:44,666
I'm sure that's just Mysterium

103
00:03:44,666 --> 00:03:46,833
being weird and Mysterium-y.

104
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:49,708
[pounding continuing]

105
00:04:01,791 --> 00:04:03,375
[moaning] Janet...

106
00:04:03,375 --> 00:04:04,500
Sorceress?

107
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,625
[groaning] Janet... Janet...

108
00:04:06,625 --> 00:04:08,916
Oh, no. Not you too.

109
00:04:08,916 --> 00:04:09,958
-[thudding]
-Whoa!

110
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:10,958
[grunting] Oof!

111
00:04:10,958 --> 00:04:11,916
What?

112
00:04:11,916 --> 00:04:12,791
[gasping]

113
00:04:15,208 --> 00:04:16,791
[Sorceress muttering]

114
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,041
Here's the deal, Riyu.

115
00:04:20,041 --> 00:04:22,291
We gotta get to Djinjago, fast,

116
00:04:22,291 --> 00:04:24,083
but we don't know where it is.

117
00:04:24,083 --> 00:04:25,333
The only times
we've been there,

118
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:26,333
we were summoned,

119
00:04:26,333 --> 00:04:27,916
or Zanth flew us...

120
00:04:27,916 --> 00:04:30,083
[Riyu grumbling eagerly]

121
00:04:30,083 --> 00:04:32,375
Looks like you're thinking
what we're thinking.

122
00:04:36,625 --> 00:04:38,625
Zanth!

123
00:04:38,625 --> 00:04:39,625
And Rontu?

124
00:04:42,166 --> 00:04:45,333
I've been helping this one
with his Ninja training.

125
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:47,791
He has shown much potential.

126
00:04:47,791 --> 00:04:49,125
[grumbling modestly]

127
00:04:49,125 --> 00:04:52,375
I anticipate
his first Spinjitzu Tornado

128
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:53,375
will be soon,

129
00:04:53,375 --> 00:04:56,458
if he keeps up his hard work.

130
00:04:56,458 --> 00:04:58,500
I just achieved
my first tornado too,

131
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,500
like, yesterday!

132
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:01,166
You can do it, buddy!

133
00:05:01,166 --> 00:05:02,166
We can do it.

134
00:05:02,166 --> 00:05:03,333
[Riyu grumbling in agreement]

135
00:05:04,375 --> 00:05:05,375
Zanth,

136
00:05:05,375 --> 00:05:07,083
you took us to Djinjago before.

137
00:05:07,083 --> 00:05:08,416
Can you do it again?

138
00:05:08,416 --> 00:05:10,125
[Zanth roaring]

139
00:05:10,125 --> 00:05:13,458
She says she feels
her homeland regrowing,

140
00:05:13,458 --> 00:05:16,500
and would love to see
what it's become.

141
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:18,166
Whoo! Let's go!

142
00:05:18,166 --> 00:05:19,416
Dibs on the front seat!

143
00:05:19,416 --> 00:05:23,208
Riyu, you should stay
and focus on your training.

144
00:05:23,208 --> 00:05:26,583
[grumbling]

145
00:05:28,083 --> 00:05:29,916
True, little one.

146
00:05:29,916 --> 00:05:31,666
Not much point in training

147
00:05:31,666 --> 00:05:33,458
if you don't save the world now.

148
00:05:34,541 --> 00:05:37,750
You have always been
a wise little dragon.

149
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:40,791
Go, but please be careful.

150
00:05:40,791 --> 00:05:42,583
[grumbling in agreement]

151
00:05:45,166 --> 00:05:46,750
[Sorceress groaning
and muttering]

152
00:05:48,208 --> 00:05:49,500
Sorceress, watch out!

153
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,541
[blades clashing]

154
00:05:50,541 --> 00:05:52,708
[zombie-like moaning]

155
00:05:53,958 --> 00:05:55,208
[grunting with effort]

156
00:05:59,041 --> 00:06:01,458
[zombie-like moaning]

157
00:06:08,625 --> 00:06:10,083
H'yah! Yaah!

158
00:06:16,166 --> 00:06:17,333
What is this thing?

159
00:06:19,875 --> 00:06:21,583
[grunting with effort]

160
00:06:25,583 --> 00:06:27,166
Had enough?

161
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:29,375
[gasping]

162
00:06:30,791 --> 00:06:31,875
H'yah! H'ah! H'ah!

163
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:36,333
Knock it off!

164
00:06:38,125 --> 00:06:39,833
Or I will!

165
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:49,416
[Sorceress moaning]

166
00:06:49,416 --> 00:06:50,625
What the--?

167
00:06:53,375 --> 00:06:55,125
Put me down, you oaf!

168
00:06:57,375 --> 00:06:58,416
Sorceress?

169
00:06:58,416 --> 00:06:59,500
Do I know you?

170
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:00,625
I'm Nya.

171
00:07:00,625 --> 00:07:02,875
We met after
the Battle of the Blood Moon.

172
00:07:02,875 --> 00:07:05,583
You helped us save
the Cloud Kingdom, remember?

173
00:07:05,583 --> 00:07:07,000
Blood Moon?

174
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,291
Cloud Kingdom?

175
00:07:08,291 --> 00:07:10,166
You're just doing words,

176
00:07:10,166 --> 00:07:12,666
trying to confuse
a kindly old coconut.

177
00:07:12,666 --> 00:07:15,333
Are you the Sorceress
or a coconut?

178
00:07:15,333 --> 00:07:19,208
Eh, a little bit of column A,
a little of column B,

179
00:07:19,208 --> 00:07:20,333
you know how it is.

180
00:07:21,250 --> 00:07:25,833
I'm a magical back-up copy
of the Sorceress's personality.

181
00:07:25,833 --> 00:07:29,916
The non-coconut Sorceress
made me a bunch of years ago,

182
00:07:29,916 --> 00:07:33,333
in case Janet's whole
mind-wipe scheme ever worked.

183
00:07:33,333 --> 00:07:35,583
[Sorceress muttering]
Janet... Janet...

184
00:07:35,583 --> 00:07:37,083
I just got activated,

185
00:07:37,083 --> 00:07:39,458
probably because that one's
pfft! right now.

186
00:07:39,458 --> 00:07:41,708
No offense!

187
00:07:41,708 --> 00:07:42,875
Janet...

188
00:07:42,875 --> 00:07:43,750
[splashing]

189
00:07:43,750 --> 00:07:44,833
Okay...

190
00:07:44,833 --> 00:07:46,958
but why a coconut?

191
00:07:46,958 --> 00:07:49,333
Good melons were out of season.

192
00:07:49,333 --> 00:07:50,916
So, what's your deal?

193
00:07:50,916 --> 00:07:52,000
Did we, uh...

194
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,916
did you and the
non-coconut Sorceress

195
00:07:53,916 --> 00:07:54,958
have plans?

196
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:57,416
Ladies' weekend? Staycation?

197
00:07:57,416 --> 00:07:58,375
[sighing]

198
00:07:58,375 --> 00:07:59,625
Long story short,

199
00:07:59,625 --> 00:08:02,791
I need to go to a place
called the Cave of Tones.

200
00:08:02,791 --> 00:08:03,791
Fast.

201
00:08:03,791 --> 00:08:04,625
Ever heard of it?

202
00:08:04,625 --> 00:08:06,583
Yeah, I'm not tone deaf.

203
00:08:06,583 --> 00:08:07,583
Pfft!

204
00:08:07,583 --> 00:08:10,208
Even as a coconut,
I've still got it!

205
00:08:10,208 --> 00:08:11,333
Uh...

206
00:08:11,333 --> 00:08:13,250
"West past Mt. Mollin"?

207
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:14,250
Yowza!

208
00:08:14,250 --> 00:08:16,958
Those directions are outdated.

209
00:08:16,958 --> 00:08:18,500
[groaning] Bleckt!

210
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:21,000
Yeah, that mountain
isn't there anymore.

211
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
Earthquake.

212
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,875
Now it's just
a vast chasm of doom.

213
00:08:24,875 --> 00:08:26,916
Where are you getting
your travel info,

214
00:08:26,916 --> 00:08:28,583
an ancient vault?

215
00:08:28,583 --> 00:08:30,500
Actually, yes.

216
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:33,333
Huh! Then it's a good thing
I'm going with you!

217
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:35,375
I will show you
a current route,

218
00:08:35,375 --> 00:08:37,166
one that won't get you killed.

219
00:08:37,166 --> 00:08:39,125
Maimed, maybe, but not killed...

220
00:08:39,125 --> 00:08:41,041
probably. Let's go!

221
00:08:42,916 --> 00:08:47,250
Janet... Janet...
Janet... Janet...

222
00:08:50,333 --> 00:08:52,083
[zombie-like moaning]

223
00:08:52,083 --> 00:08:53,250
[gasping]

224
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:54,250
Oh no!

225
00:08:54,250 --> 00:08:56,291
Not you too, Cole!

226
00:08:56,291 --> 00:08:59,250
He fought hard to free
the Finders' souls, but...

227
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:00,500
Come on.

228
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:01,416
I've got you.

229
00:09:01,416 --> 00:09:02,416
Wyldfyre!

230
00:09:02,416 --> 00:09:03,791
-Flame fist!
-Flame fist!

231
00:09:03,791 --> 00:09:05,833
And look who I brought.

232
00:09:05,833 --> 00:09:07,500
Sora?

233
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:09,916
Hey. I'm back.

234
00:09:17,916 --> 00:09:19,916
Sora, I couldn't sleep,
I was so worried about you.

235
00:09:19,916 --> 00:09:20,875
You were?

236
00:09:20,875 --> 00:09:22,125
Well, I mean...

237
00:09:22,125 --> 00:09:23,416
we all were, not just me.

238
00:09:23,416 --> 00:09:25,416
I'm sure others couldn't sleep--

239
00:09:25,416 --> 00:09:27,041
Where's Arin?

240
00:09:27,041 --> 00:09:28,750
Uh, with Lloyd.

241
00:09:28,750 --> 00:09:30,875
Look, as you probably
know already,

242
00:09:30,875 --> 00:09:33,166
the Merged Realms
have a big problem,

243
00:09:33,166 --> 00:09:34,666
and we need to help.

244
00:09:36,208 --> 00:09:38,250
What do we have to do?

245
00:09:39,375 --> 00:09:42,708
[distant thunder rumbling]

246
00:09:42,708 --> 00:09:44,250
[panting]
...and after the Merge,

247
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:47,541
all us Ninja
ended up in different places.

248
00:09:47,541 --> 00:09:49,000
Did you find each other?

249
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,791
Yeah, but...

250
00:09:50,791 --> 00:09:52,708
I'm not sure
that was a good thing.

251
00:09:52,708 --> 00:09:54,791
Ooh, this sounds juicy,

252
00:09:54,791 --> 00:09:55,916
and I would know.

253
00:09:55,916 --> 00:09:56,875
I'm a coconut.

254
00:09:56,875 --> 00:09:57,791
Go on.

255
00:09:58,958 --> 00:10:00,333
[gasping]

256
00:10:05,083 --> 00:10:06,041
Oh.

257
00:10:06,041 --> 00:10:07,625
Well, this shouldn't be here.

258
00:10:07,625 --> 00:10:09,583
Then why is it here?

259
00:10:09,583 --> 00:10:11,083
You led me to a dead end!

260
00:10:11,083 --> 00:10:14,291
Magical lands sometimes change
for no reason.

261
00:10:14,291 --> 00:10:15,583
How am I supposed to know?

262
00:10:15,583 --> 00:10:17,416
I'm a backup coconut!

263
00:10:20,291 --> 00:10:21,250
[gasping]

264
00:10:21,250 --> 00:10:23,250
Can I cross on those?

265
00:10:23,250 --> 00:10:25,541
Yes... and no.

266
00:10:25,541 --> 00:10:29,041
The Mercurial Mushrooms
aren't always the most stable.

267
00:10:29,041 --> 00:10:31,583
It's the only option we have.

268
00:10:33,791 --> 00:10:35,250
Uh... so you were saying

269
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:38,833
getting the Ninja back together
wasn't a good thing?

270
00:10:38,833 --> 00:10:39,916
Yeah.

271
00:10:39,916 --> 00:10:41,791
Jay... I...

272
00:10:41,791 --> 00:10:43,875
We were together, before,

273
00:10:43,875 --> 00:10:46,500
but when I found him,
he lost his memory...

274
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,666
[grunting with effort]

275
00:10:47,666 --> 00:10:49,500
...and he was a totally
different person.

276
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,416
I thought if we could
just spend time together,

277
00:10:51,416 --> 00:10:52,291
he'd remember, but...

278
00:10:52,291 --> 00:10:54,625
Hup! ...it didn't work.

279
00:10:54,625 --> 00:10:57,250
How can people change like that?

280
00:10:57,250 --> 00:10:58,625
H'yah! Whoa!

281
00:10:58,625 --> 00:11:00,000
[grunting with effort]

282
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,541
Oh, people change, sister.

283
00:11:03,541 --> 00:11:05,791
I had someone close,

284
00:11:05,791 --> 00:11:06,916
a BFF.

285
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:09,500
We did everything together,

286
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:11,333
studied, traveled,

287
00:11:11,333 --> 00:11:13,625
sang in the same
a capella group.

288
00:11:13,625 --> 00:11:16,291
I was the beatboxer!

289
00:11:16,291 --> 00:11:18,250
♪ Boots, cats, cats and boots ♪

290
00:11:18,250 --> 00:11:19,875
♪ Boots and cats
Cats and boots ♪

291
00:11:19,875 --> 00:11:20,958
But...

292
00:11:20,958 --> 00:11:24,000
over time,
our priorities changed.

293
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,416
I was still focused
on the magic, the people,

294
00:11:26,416 --> 00:11:27,708
friendships,

295
00:11:27,708 --> 00:11:31,291
but all he cared about
was more and more wealth.

296
00:11:31,291 --> 00:11:33,833
I imagine he was another
magic-wielder like you, right?

297
00:11:33,833 --> 00:11:37,125
Hup! Someone you could
share everything with?

298
00:11:37,125 --> 00:11:39,000
Yeah... something like that.

299
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,666
[gasping] Whoa!

300
00:11:40,666 --> 00:11:42,000
[panting]

301
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,375
[grunting with effort]

302
00:11:43,375 --> 00:11:44,416
[yelping] Oh!

303
00:11:45,416 --> 00:11:48,041
I don't see how we're both
making it out of this.

304
00:11:48,041 --> 00:11:49,166
Let me go!

305
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:50,958
I'm just a coconut copy.

306
00:11:50,958 --> 00:11:52,166
No way!

307
00:11:52,166 --> 00:11:55,000
Ninja have this whole thing
about not quitting.

308
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,083
[grunting with effort]

309
00:11:58,208 --> 00:11:59,125
H'yah!

310
00:12:01,375 --> 00:12:03,791
Ah... h'yah!

311
00:12:04,625 --> 00:12:06,708
Phew! [panting]

312
00:12:06,708 --> 00:12:09,083
Let's hope there are
no more surprises like that.

313
00:12:09,083 --> 00:12:10,541
This is Mysterium.

314
00:12:10,541 --> 00:12:12,541
Nothing but surprises.

315
00:12:19,125 --> 00:12:21,625
[grumble talking]

316
00:12:21,625 --> 00:12:23,916
[Wyldfyre] Whee!

317
00:12:26,375 --> 00:12:27,833
Are we there yet?

318
00:12:27,833 --> 00:12:29,833
How far away is this place?

319
00:12:29,833 --> 00:12:32,291
Frak, Zanth is doing her best.

320
00:12:32,291 --> 00:12:35,750
We'll get to Djinjago
when we get to Djinjago!

321
00:12:35,750 --> 00:12:38,000
But time is, like,
of the essence.

322
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,625
Then let's sing
to pass the time!

323
00:12:40,625 --> 00:12:44,000
♪ Oh... what do you do
with a sleepy Ninja? ♪

324
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,916
♪ What do you do with
a sleepy Ninja? ♪

325
00:12:45,916 --> 00:12:46,875
♪ What do you-- ♪

326
00:12:46,875 --> 00:12:47,833
Why don't we practice

327
00:12:47,833 --> 00:12:49,125
the melody Bleckt taught us?

328
00:12:49,125 --> 00:12:50,666
We're gonna need to play it
on the bells

329
00:12:50,666 --> 00:12:52,500
to awaken
our half of the Arc Dragon.

330
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:56,291
[singing melody]

331
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:05,125
[Frak harmonizing]

332
00:13:05,125 --> 00:13:09,458
[singing]

333
00:13:09,458 --> 00:13:11,000
Please don't harmonize.

334
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,250
We've got to remember
the primary notes,

335
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:15,041
and that just makes it harder.

336
00:13:15,041 --> 00:13:17,916
Sorry, I just habitually
harmonize in thirds.

337
00:13:17,916 --> 00:13:20,125
Years of vocal training.

338
00:13:20,125 --> 00:13:21,583
[rolling lips] Brrr... ah!

339
00:13:21,583 --> 00:13:22,625
Okay, I'm warm.

340
00:13:22,625 --> 00:13:23,500
From the one, please?

341
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:27,083
[singing melody in unison]

342
00:13:27,083 --> 00:13:30,833
[♪♪♪]

343
00:13:30,833 --> 00:13:33,041
[singing loudly and out of tune]

344
00:13:33,041 --> 00:13:35,875
[grumbling in protest]

345
00:13:35,875 --> 00:13:38,625
[singing loudly]

346
00:13:38,625 --> 00:13:39,750
[gasping]

347
00:13:39,750 --> 00:13:42,291
Let's add words for funzies!

348
00:13:42,291 --> 00:13:45,208
I've been super into
sea shanties lately.

349
00:13:45,208 --> 00:13:48,166
♪ Yo-ho, the ocean calls! ♪

350
00:13:48,166 --> 00:13:51,708
♪ The Ninja kicks
and the bad guys fall! ♪

351
00:13:51,708 --> 00:13:53,625
We cannot let her
ring the bells.

352
00:13:53,625 --> 00:13:54,833
[Wyldfyre] I heard that!

353
00:13:54,833 --> 00:13:57,625
Not my fault you can't
appreciate a good shanty.

354
00:13:57,625 --> 00:13:59,416
Let's play the Quiet Game.
One, two, three, go!

355
00:14:02,708 --> 00:14:03,541
[groaning]

356
00:14:03,541 --> 00:14:04,791
Who wants snacks?

357
00:14:04,791 --> 00:14:06,291
I mean, I didn't bring
any snacks.

358
00:14:06,291 --> 00:14:07,833
Why would I say that?

359
00:14:07,833 --> 00:14:09,458
[rummaging]

360
00:14:09,458 --> 00:14:11,875
[munching]
Okay, but seriously,

361
00:14:11,875 --> 00:14:13,500
are we there yet?

362
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:14,958
Time is of the essence.

363
00:14:14,958 --> 00:14:16,125
Zanth, my friend,

364
00:14:16,125 --> 00:14:17,625
can you sense Djinjago?

365
00:14:17,625 --> 00:14:18,875
Are we getting closer?

366
00:14:18,875 --> 00:14:20,375
[growling]

367
00:14:20,375 --> 00:14:21,583
[Frak] Was that a yes?

368
00:14:21,583 --> 00:14:22,541
[all] Whoa!

369
00:14:25,958 --> 00:14:27,291
[grumbling]

370
00:14:28,125 --> 00:14:30,416
[gasping]
Are you okay, girl?

371
00:14:30,416 --> 00:14:31,500
Wha-hoo!

372
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,708
I don't even know
what's happening,

373
00:14:33,708 --> 00:14:36,583
but this is awesome!

374
00:14:37,833 --> 00:14:40,083
[all yelping]

375
00:14:40,083 --> 00:14:42,708
Zanth, what is going on here?

376
00:14:44,291 --> 00:14:45,708
Whoa!

377
00:14:45,708 --> 00:14:48,208
[roaring]

378
00:14:48,208 --> 00:14:49,916
[grunting with impact]

379
00:14:49,916 --> 00:14:51,125
[gasping]

380
00:14:51,125 --> 00:14:51,958
Whoa!

381
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,750
Does she normally
do stuff like this?

382
00:14:54,750 --> 00:14:57,250
She got really big once before,

383
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:58,833
but it wasn't like this.

384
00:14:58,833 --> 00:15:00,958
Zanth, quite a glow-up,

385
00:15:00,958 --> 00:15:03,708
but what brought this on
right-- aah!

386
00:15:03,708 --> 00:15:05,375
[grumbling wearily]

387
00:15:05,375 --> 00:15:07,208
[all yelping] Ah!
No, no, no!

388
00:15:07,208 --> 00:15:08,375
[groaning]

389
00:15:08,375 --> 00:15:09,708
Djinjago!

390
00:15:09,708 --> 00:15:11,208
We made it!

391
00:15:11,208 --> 00:15:13,291
[♪♪♪]

392
00:15:19,083 --> 00:15:20,958
[ThunderFang roaring]

393
00:15:25,541 --> 00:15:30,083
<i>Someone is nearing</i>
<i>the Arc Dragon of Focus.</i>

394
00:15:30,083 --> 00:15:31,583
<i>The Ninja...</i>

395
00:15:31,583 --> 00:15:36,500
<i>They dare attempt to awaken</i>
<i>my eternal enemy?</i>

396
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,500
[grumbling]

397
00:15:45,166 --> 00:15:46,458
Whoa...

398
00:15:46,458 --> 00:15:47,875
I had no idea

399
00:15:47,875 --> 00:15:51,291
Djinjago would've
grown this much so fast,

400
00:15:51,291 --> 00:15:53,750
and it looks like Arrakore
moved it over the water.

401
00:15:54,875 --> 00:15:56,166
[groaning]

402
00:15:56,166 --> 00:15:57,541
[kissing]

403
00:15:57,541 --> 00:16:00,000
Look at all this!

404
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,291
New towers, and fountains?

405
00:16:05,541 --> 00:16:07,583
Is that a Monastery
portal gate?

406
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:14,750
So much has changed,
and it's all so majestic.

407
00:16:14,750 --> 00:16:16,958
-[yelping]
-Glad you like it!

408
00:16:16,958 --> 00:16:18,541
Arrakore!

409
00:16:18,541 --> 00:16:20,416
Sora!

410
00:16:20,416 --> 00:16:21,458
Riyu!

411
00:16:21,458 --> 00:16:22,500
[grumbling happily]

412
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:24,625
Oh, I do love when you visit!

413
00:16:24,625 --> 00:16:26,791
So good to see you again!

414
00:16:26,791 --> 00:16:28,000
[grumbling happily]

415
00:16:29,291 --> 00:16:30,708
And you brought friends!

416
00:16:34,291 --> 00:16:36,333
Zanth, is that you?

417
00:16:36,333 --> 00:16:37,291
[growling]

418
00:16:37,291 --> 00:16:39,250
Look at you!

419
00:16:39,250 --> 00:16:41,583
I knew my work
expanding Djinjago

420
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:43,375
would have amazing results,

421
00:16:43,375 --> 00:16:44,750
but I never expected

422
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:47,083
it would infuse
a Djinjagan dragon

423
00:16:47,083 --> 00:16:48,708
with such energy!

424
00:16:58,416 --> 00:17:00,541
There it is, Freebooters.

425
00:17:00,541 --> 00:17:02,458
Djinjago.

426
00:17:02,458 --> 00:17:06,458
Rapton never doesn't find
what he wants.

427
00:17:07,875 --> 00:17:09,166
Shouldn't it be

428
00:17:09,166 --> 00:17:13,000
"Rapton always finds
what he wants?"

429
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,083
[Rapton] What's that?!

430
00:17:14,083 --> 00:17:16,125
Is someone questionalating

431
00:17:16,125 --> 00:17:19,333
Rapton's grammaticalism
masteritude?

432
00:17:19,333 --> 00:17:21,750
No, of course not.

433
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:23,458
[snarling]

434
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:30,333
[sighing wearily]

435
00:17:30,333 --> 00:17:31,666
We're here!

436
00:17:34,958 --> 00:17:36,958
Wow...

437
00:17:36,958 --> 00:17:39,666
but we need a Cave of Tones.

438
00:17:39,666 --> 00:17:41,166
It's behind the water!

439
00:17:41,166 --> 00:17:42,250
Let's go!

440
00:17:42,250 --> 00:17:43,791
We just need to play the tones

441
00:17:43,791 --> 00:17:45,416
in the order this Blecky--

442
00:17:45,416 --> 00:17:46,416
Bleckt.

443
00:17:46,416 --> 00:17:47,958
Bleckt? Really?

444
00:17:47,958 --> 00:17:49,750
Sounds like someone barfing.

445
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:52,500
His parents didn't do him
any favors with that name.

446
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:55,083
Anyhoosy, we do
what he told you,

447
00:17:55,083 --> 00:17:58,625
then badda-bing, we awaken
the half Arc Dragon of Focus

448
00:17:58,625 --> 00:18:01,166
and save the world! Na-na!

449
00:18:01,166 --> 00:18:04,041
Only if the other Ninja
pull off their parts too.

450
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:05,958
Oh, you don't think they will?

451
00:18:05,958 --> 00:18:07,541
They've never
let me down before.

452
00:18:07,541 --> 00:18:08,958
Ah, sounds like you've got

453
00:18:08,958 --> 00:18:11,458
a pretty good group of friends
behind you.

454
00:18:11,458 --> 00:18:13,583
Now, come on, let's do this!

455
00:18:13,583 --> 00:18:15,583
[heavy footsteps]

456
00:18:15,583 --> 00:18:17,166
[gasping] Oh, no...

457
00:18:19,166 --> 00:18:20,166
Great.

458
00:18:20,166 --> 00:18:22,291
More Mysterium surprises?

459
00:18:24,125 --> 00:18:26,708
Who disturbs Powerlid,

460
00:18:26,708 --> 00:18:28,458
the ultimate cyclops,

461
00:18:28,458 --> 00:18:32,625
also known as the ultimate
object of admiration?

462
00:18:32,625 --> 00:18:34,750
Ugh... pretend I'm not here.

463
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:36,041
Hide me in a tree,

464
00:18:36,041 --> 00:18:38,166
I'm just your regular
run-of-the-mill coconut.

465
00:18:38,166 --> 00:18:39,625
Do you know that cyclops?

466
00:18:39,625 --> 00:18:40,625
No!

467
00:18:40,625 --> 00:18:42,666
Yes! I do. I did.

468
00:18:42,666 --> 00:18:45,500
Yeah, but I never thought
I'd run into him again.

469
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:47,416
Wait, is this...?

470
00:18:47,416 --> 00:18:50,333
The former BFF
I was talking about? Yes!

471
00:18:50,333 --> 00:18:52,458
And it looks like
becoming a greedy guts

472
00:18:52,458 --> 00:18:55,708
didn't amount to much
if he lives in a cave.

473
00:18:55,708 --> 00:18:56,666
Serves him right.

474
00:18:56,666 --> 00:18:59,125
Ugh, another one
of you Ninjerks

475
00:18:59,125 --> 00:19:01,750
here to steal Powerlid's stuff!

476
00:19:01,750 --> 00:19:05,166
Time to grind your bones
into powder

477
00:19:05,166 --> 00:19:06,666
like Powerlid does best!

478
00:19:07,625 --> 00:19:08,583
[growling]

479
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:13,875
Here you go.

480
00:19:13,875 --> 00:19:16,833
Some aged spore-rot broth.

481
00:19:16,833 --> 00:19:22,083
Auntie Croakwart's old recipe,
yum, yum, yum!

482
00:19:22,083 --> 00:19:24,000
[gagging and groaning]

483
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,208
I'll be honest,

484
00:19:25,208 --> 00:19:28,250
the flavor's, uh,
a little bit on the sharp side.

485
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:29,416
[sniffing]

486
00:19:29,416 --> 00:19:30,458
[coughing]

487
00:19:30,458 --> 00:19:31,583
[fly buzzing]

488
00:19:31,583 --> 00:19:33,375
Are you sure
that's even safe to eat?

489
00:19:33,375 --> 00:19:35,708
It smells rank...

490
00:19:35,708 --> 00:19:37,500
and I live
in a wasteland of junk.

491
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:40,791
It's very nourishing
and healing...

492
00:19:40,791 --> 00:19:42,541
if you can keep it down.

493
00:19:42,541 --> 00:19:44,625
Well, if nothing else,

494
00:19:44,625 --> 00:19:47,333
maybe the... smell
will revive them.

495
00:19:47,333 --> 00:19:50,166
Don't worry,
I've got plenty left.

496
00:19:50,166 --> 00:19:52,041
[fly buzzing]

497
00:19:57,041 --> 00:19:58,041
Oh.

498
00:19:58,041 --> 00:19:59,541
Does she not eat?

499
00:19:59,541 --> 00:20:01,875
No, she eats all the time.

500
00:20:01,875 --> 00:20:03,333
Well, how does...?

501
00:20:03,333 --> 00:20:04,458
Um...

502
00:20:04,458 --> 00:20:06,041
I mean, where does the food...?

503
00:20:06,041 --> 00:20:07,333
[stammering]

504
00:20:07,333 --> 00:20:09,791
Of all the questions
I need answers to right now,

505
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:11,541
that's very far down the list.

506
00:20:11,541 --> 00:20:13,750
Cole? Can you hear me?

507
00:20:13,750 --> 00:20:14,625
It's Geo.

508
00:20:14,625 --> 00:20:16,666
[moaning]

509
00:20:16,666 --> 00:20:18,166
What can I do?

510
00:20:18,166 --> 00:20:19,666
Can you...

511
00:20:19,666 --> 00:20:22,041
blink twice
if you can understand me?

512
00:20:22,041 --> 00:20:24,750
[moaning]

513
00:20:27,541 --> 00:20:29,166
[portal powering up]

514
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:30,875
Who's coming now?

515
00:20:30,875 --> 00:20:33,041
If the Ninja are back
this fast,

516
00:20:33,041 --> 00:20:35,125
it probably means
something went wrong.

517
00:20:42,375 --> 00:20:44,041
No, no!

518
00:20:44,041 --> 00:20:45,916
Well, he can't be here!

519
00:20:45,916 --> 00:20:47,916
How can he be here?!

520
00:20:54,791 --> 00:20:56,333
Don't get any closer!

521
00:20:56,333 --> 00:21:00,291
The Ninja are scattered
across the Merged Lands.

522
00:21:00,291 --> 00:21:03,750
Save yourself
the pain and suffering.

523
00:21:03,750 --> 00:21:05,666
Submit.

524
00:21:05,666 --> 00:21:07,500
You can't intimidate us.

525
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:08,916
Ninja never quit.

526
00:21:08,916 --> 00:21:11,000
You are not Ninja.

527
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:14,416
We're... Ninja-adjacent,

528
00:21:14,416 --> 00:21:17,791
and Ninja-adjacent
never quit either.

529
00:21:19,166 --> 00:21:21,291
So be it.

530
00:21:24,083 --> 00:21:25,083
Eat this!

531
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:27,500
[gagging]

532
00:21:32,916 --> 00:21:34,208
[spluttering]

533
00:21:34,208 --> 00:21:35,916
[screaming in rage]

534
00:21:39,708 --> 00:21:41,750
[groaning fearfully]

535
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:42,625
[tapping button]

536
00:21:43,708 --> 00:21:44,583
[roaring]

537
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

